  {
   "id": 335736,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/2a5eac34ab71b5df.jpg\" alt=\"A diagram shows a patient’s arm, with an arrow representing blood leading from the arm to a dialyzer. In the dialyzer, the waste in the blood is drawn through a semipermeable membrane toward a compartment filled with fresh dialysate. The used dialysate then flows to a collecting bottle. The clean blood is returned to the patient’s same arm.\"></p>\n\n<p>Patients with kidney illnesses use dialysis machines to remove harmful urea from their blood. The blood is separated from a solution, called the dialysate, that is designed to remove wastes by diffusion through a semipermeable membrane. The semipermeable membrane is likely permeable to _____ and impermeable to _____.</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 848528,
     "content_html": "red blood cells, urea"
    },
    {
     "id": 848527,
     "content_html": "dialysate, blood plasma"
    },
    {
     "id": 848526,
     "content_html": "blood plasma, urea"
    },
    {
     "id": 848529,
     "content_html": "urea, red blood cells"
    }
   ],
